{"seq":1,"slug":"the-theory-of-forms","title":"The Theory Of Forms","docCount":2,"url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/plato/core-contributions/the-theory-of-forms","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"the-world-of-forms","title":"理念的世界","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/plato/core-contributions/the-theory-of-forms/the-world-of-forms","wordCount":2355,"readingTime":10},{"seq":2,"slug":"the-allegory-of-the-cave","title":"洞穴之喻","url":"/l-doc-books/c/people/plato/core-contributions/the-theory-of-forms/the-allegory-of-the-cave","wordCount":1859,"readingTime":8}],"introMarkdown":"本章呈现柏拉图哲学的核心——理念论。柏拉图区分了变动不居的可感世界与永恒完美的理念世界，主张理念才是真正的实在，可感事物则\"分有\"或\"摹仿\"着理念。而著名的\"洞穴之喻\"，则以被囚于洞穴、只见影子的囚徒走出洞穴的故事，生动地阐明了从现象到理念、从黑暗到光明的哲学上升之路。本章揭示理念论作为西方形而上学基石的深远意义。\n"}